{"cuisine/kashmiri-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/kashmiri-cuisine","n":"Kashmiri cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["North Indian cuisine","cuisine/north-indian-cuisine"],["Pakistani cuisine","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Kashmiri cuisine is the traditional culinary practices of the Kashmiri people. Rice has been a staple food in Kashmir since ancient times. The equivalent for the phrase \"bread and butter\" in the Kashmiri language is haakh-batte (greens and rice)."],["Kashmiri cuisine is generally meat-heavy. The region has, per capita, the highest mutton consumers in the Indian Subcontinent. Lamb or sheep is the preferred choice of meat amongst Pandits, whereas Muslims prefer goats."],["In a majority of Kashmiri cooking, bread is not part of the meal. Bread is generally only eaten with tea in the morning, afternoon and evening. The cooking methods of vegetables, mutton, homemade cheese (paneer), and legumes by Muslims are similar to those of Pandits, except in the use of onions, garlic and shallots by Muslims in place of asafoetida. Cockscomb flower, called \"mawal\" in Kashmiri, is boiled to prepare a red food colouring, as used in certain dishes mostly in Wazwan. Kashmiri Pandit cuisine uses the mildly pungent Kashmiri red chili powder as a spice, as well as ratanjot to impart colour to certain dishes like rogan josh. Kashmiri Muslim cuisine uses chilies in moderate quantity, and avoid hot dishes at large meals. In Kashmiri Muslim cuisine, vegetable curries are common with meat traditionally considered an expensive indulgence. Wazwan dishes with rice, some vegetables and salad are prepared for weddings and special occasions like Eid."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"kashmiri-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kashmiri_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Goshtaab","dish/goshtaab"],["Katlam","dish/katlam"],["Wazwan","dish/wazwan"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"iKashmir Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ikashmir.net","note":"Kashmiri Pandit community site with a collection of traditional recipes.","url":"https://ikashmir.net/cookbook/recipes/index.html","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"On the Himalayan Trail: Recipes and Stories from Kashmir to Ladakh","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Romy Gill, 2022","note":"Kashmiri and Ladakhi recipes gathered by a British Indian chef.","url":"https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/466438/on-the-himalayan-trail-by-romy-gill/9781784885083","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781784884406"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Goshtaab","ingredient/goshtaab"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Rogan josh","ingredient/rogan-josh"],["Seekh kebab","ingredient/seekh-kebab"],["Tabak maaz","ingredient/tabak-maaz"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["North Indian cuisine","cuisine/north-indian-cuisine"],["Pakistani cuisine","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/49/Kashmiri_Wazwan.jpg/500px-Kashmiri_Wazwan.jpg","w":500,"h":624,"by":"Draabidwani1","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kashmiri_Wazwan.jpg"}},"cuisine/telugu-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/telugu-cuisine","n":"Telugu cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["South Indian cuisine","cuisine/south-indian-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Andhra cuisine is the traditional culinary style of the Telugu people, who are native to the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. It is generally known for its tangy, hot, and spicy taste."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"telugu-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telugu_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Mahanandi","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"nandyala.org","note":"Indira's long-running blog of Andhra vegetarian home cooking.","url":"https://nandyala.org/mahanandi/archives/2006/12/12/cooking-at-home-with-pedatha-cookbook-review-interview-and-recipe/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Spice Up The Curry (Andhra)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spiceupthecurry.com","note":"Andhra section of Kanan Patel's Indian vegetarian recipe blog.","url":"https://www.spiceupthecurry.com/category/recipes-by-region/andhra-recipe/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Five Morsels of Love","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Archana Pidathala","note":"Telugu family recipes adapted from the author's grandmother's cookbook.","url":"","suggested":true},{"name":"Cooking at Home with Pedatha: Vegetarian Recipes from a Traditional Andhra Kitchen","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Jigyasa Giri and Pratibha Jain","note":"Traditional Andhra vegetarian recipes recorded from an elder home cook.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["South Indian cuisine","cuisine/south-indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Telugu cooking","count":2,"links":[["Andhra cuisine","cuisine/andhra-cuisine"],["Hyderabadi cuisine","cuisine/hyderabadi-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/3e/Vegetarian_Andhra_Meal.jpg/500px-Vegetarian_Andhra_Meal.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"PriyaBooks","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vegetarian_Andhra_Meal.jpg"}},"cuisine/greek-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/greek-cuisine","n":"Greek cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Greece","intro":[["Greek cuisine is the cuisine of Greece and the Greek diaspora. In common with many other cuisines of the Mediterranean, it is founded on the triad  of wheat, olive oil, and wine. It uses vegetables, olive oil, grains, fish, and meat, including pork, poultry, veal and beef, lamb, rabbit, and goat. Other important ingredients include pasta (such as hilopites), cheeses, herbs, lemon juice, olives and olive oil, and yogurt. Bread made of wheat is ubiquitous; other grains, notably barley, are also used, especially for paximathia. Common dessert ingredients include nuts, honey, fruits, sesame, and filo pastries. It continues traditions from Ancient Greek and Byzantine cuisine, while incorporating Middle Eastern, Balkan, and Italian influences."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"greek-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greek_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":20,"links":[["Avgolemono","dish/avgolemono"],["Baba ghanoush","dish/baba-ghanoush"],["Bouyiourdi","dish/bouyiourdi"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Diples","dish/diples"],["Fasolada","dish/fasolada"],["Freddo cappuccino","dish/freddo-cappuccino"],["Greek restaurant","dish/greek-restaurant"],["Greek salad","dish/greek-salad"],["İmam bayıldı","dish/imam-bay-ld"],["Kakavia (soup)","dish/kakavia-soup"],["Kalitsounia","dish/kalitsounia"],["Karydopita","dish/karydopita"],["Keşkek","dish/keskek"],["Ladera","dish/ladera"],["Noumboulo","dish/noumboulo"],["Psarosoupa","dish/psarosoupa"],["Spanakorizo","dish/spanakorizo"],["Taramasalata","dish/taramasalata"],["Tzatziki","dish/tzatziki"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Dimitra's Dishes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dimitrasdishes.com","note":"Dimitra Alfieris's video channel and blog focused on classic Greek home cooking.","url":"https://dimitrasdishes.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":3,"rows":[{"name":"The Greek Kitchen","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Vefa Alexiadou","note":"Phaidon collection of Greek recipes from Greece's best-known television cook.","url":"https://www.phaidon.com/products/the-greek-kitchen","suggested":true},{"name":"My Greek Table","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Diane Kochilas, 2018","note":"Companion book to Kochilas's public television series on Greek home cooking.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781250166371","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781250166371"},{"name":"Ikaria","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Diane Kochilas, 2014","note":"Recipes and food traditions of the Greek island of Ikaria.","url":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/593549/ikaria-by-diane-kochilas-photography-by-vassillis-stenos","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Feta","ingredient/feta"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Tahini","ingredient/tahini"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"],["Cabbage","ingredient/cabbage"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Common bean","ingredient/common-bean"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Kalamata olive","ingredient/kalamata-olive"],["Olive","ingredient/olive"],["Oregano","ingredient/oregano"],["Aubergine","ingredient/aubergine"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Greek cooking","count":7,"links":[["Cappadocian Greek cuisine","cuisine/cappadocian-greeks-cuisine"],["Cretan cuisine","cuisine/cretan-cuisine"],["Cuisine of the Ionian Islands","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-ionian-islands"],["Cypriot cuisine","cuisine/cypriot-cuisine"],["Epirotic cuisine","cuisine/epirotic-cuisine"],["Macedonian cuisine (Greek)","cuisine/macedonian-cuisine-greek"],["Pontic Greek cuisine","cuisine/pontic-greek-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/01/Grk2020.jpg/500px-Grk2020.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"LIttleGreekFreshGrill","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grk2020.jpg"}},"dish/banana-roll":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/banana-roll","n":"Banana roll","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Banana roll or banana cake is a common Chinese pastry found in Hong Kong, and may occasionally be found in some overseas Chinatowns. The pastry is soft and made with glutinous rice. Ingredients may vary depending on location. Each roll or cake is a banana oil flavored circular tube or flat object, slightly bigger than an adult sized index finger, thus resembling banana. Sometimes it may have a cinnamon swirl filling. At other times it may have a filling that consists of a very ripe banana diced finely. Occasionally the more traditional red bean paste may be used."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-banana-roll"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana_roll"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Glutinous rice","ingredient/glutinous-rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Red House Spice","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Dongpo pork","dish/dongpo-pork"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edible-bird-s-nest"],["Fuqi feipian","dish/fuqi-feipian"],["Gaifan","dish/gaifan"],["Goubuli","dish/goubuli"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Hog maw","dish/hog-maw"],["Hong dou tang","dish/hong-dou-tang"],["Hot dry noodles","dish/hot-dry-noodles"],["Hot pot","dish/hot-pot"],["Huangqiao sesame cake","dish/huangqiao-sesame-cake"],["Imitation shark fin soup","dish/imitation-shark-fin-soup"],["Jiaozi","dish/jiaozi"],["Jiuqu","dish/jiuqu"],["Kung Pao chicken","dish/kung-pao-chicken"],["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"],["Liangfen","dish/liangfen"],["Lo mai chi","dish/lo-mai-chi"],["Mao xue wang","dish/mao-xue-wang"],["Mapo tofu","dish/mapo-tofu"],["Mianwo","dish/mianwo"],["Miso soup","dish/miso-soup"],["Orange cuttlefish","dish/orange-cuttlefish"],["Osmanthus cake","dish/osmanthus-cake"],["Pickled egg","dish/pickled-egg"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Red braised pork belly","dish/red-braised-pork-belly"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fb/Chinese_Banana_Roll.jpg/500px-Chinese_Banana_Roll.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Ahleong","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chinese_Banana_Roll.jpg"}},"ingredient/anchovy":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/anchovy","n":"Anchovy","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 8 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["Anchovies are small, common forage fish of the family Engraulidae. Most species are found in marine waters, but several will enter brackish water, and some in South America are restricted to fresh water."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-anchovy"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchovy"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Kapurung","dish/kapurung"],["Nasi kucing","dish/nasi-kucing"],["Sambal tuktuk","dish/sambal-tuktuk"],["Tumpeng","dish/tumpeng"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"]]],["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence",[["Green goddess dressing","dish/green-goddess-dressing"]]],["Cuisine of California","cuisine/cuisine-of-california",[["Green goddess dressing","dish/green-goddess-dressing"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"]]],["Javanese cuisine","cuisine/javanese-cuisine",[["Buntil","dish/buntil"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Shrimp paste","ingredient/shrimp-paste"],["Bamboo shoot","ingredient/bamboo-shoot"],["Bean curd","ingredient/bean-curd"],["Bumbu (seasoning)","ingredient/bumbu-seasoning"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Carrots","ingredient/carrots"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Dried shrimp","ingredient/dried-shrimp"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0f/Anchovy_closeup.jpg/500px-Anchovy_closeup.jpg","w":500,"h":325,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anchovy_closeup.jpg"}},"ingredient/bottle-gourd":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/bottle-gourd","n":"Bottle gourd","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Calabash is a vine in the family Cucurbitaceae which is grown for its fruit. It is native to tropical Africa, and cultivated across the tropics. It can be either harvested young to be consumed as a vegetable, or harvested mature to be dried and used as a kitchen utensil (typically as a ladle or bowl), beverage container or a musical instrument. When it is fresh, the fruit has a light green smooth skin and white flesh. It is also known as bottle gourd, white-flowered gourd, long melon, birdhouse gourd, New Guinea bean, New Guinea butter bean or Tasmania bean."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-bottle-gourd"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottle_gourd"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Handvo","dish/handvo"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Lentils","ingredient/lentils"],["Sesame","ingredient/sesame"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a2/Courge_encore_verte.jpg/500px-Courge_encore_verte.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"撮影者はカールおじさんです。","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Courge_encore_verte.jpg"}},"ingredient/buttercream":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/buttercream","n":"Buttercream","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Buttercream, also referred to as butter icing or butter frosting, is a type of icing used for either filling, coating or decorating cakes. The main ingredients are butter and some type of sugar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-buttercream"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buttercream"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Armenian cuisine","cuisine/armenian-cuisine",[["Mikado cake","dish/mikado-cake"]]],["Soviet cuisine","cuisine/soviet-cuisine",[["Leningradsky cake","dish/leningradsky-cake"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cocoa powder","ingredient/cocoa-powder"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Sponge cake","ingredient/sponge-cake"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/da/Chocolate_Cupcakes_with_Raspberry_Buttercream.jpg/500px-Chocolate_Cupcakes_with_Raspberry_Buttercream.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Whitney","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chocolate_Cupcakes_with_Raspberry_Buttercream.jpg"}},"dish/meju":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/meju","n":"Meju","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Korean cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Meju is a brick of dried fermented soybeans. While not consumed on its own, it serves as the basis of several Korean condiments, such as doenjang (soybean paste), ganjang (soy sauce), and gochujang (chili paste). Meju is produced by pounding, kneading, and shaping cooked soybeans, and undergoes fermentation with Aspergillus oryzae and/or Bacillus subtilis."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-meju"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meju"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Korean cuisine","cuisine/korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Maangchi","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"maangchi.com","note":"Maangchi's Korean recipe site and YouTube channel, one of the best known English sources for Korean cooking.","url":"https://www.maangchi.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Korean Bapsang","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Korean cuisine","links":[["Bap (rice dish)","dish/bap-rice-dish"],["Bibim-guksu","dish/bibim-guksu"],["Bibimbap","dish/bibimbap"],["Bosintang","dish/bosintang"],["Cheonggukjang","dish/cheonggukjang"],["Doenjang","dish/doenjang"],["Garak-guksu","dish/garak-guksu"],["Gochujang","dish/gochujang"],["Gopchang","dish/gopchang"],["Hwajeon","dish/hwajeon"],["Jijimi","dish/jijimi"],["Jokbal","dish/jokbal"],["Korean restaurant","dish/korean-restaurant"],["Maekjeok","dish/maekjeok"],["Maeun-tang","dish/maeun-tang"],["Makchang","dish/makchang"],["Mandu-guk","dish/mandu-guk"],["Mandu-gwa","dish/mandu-gwa"],["Meat jun","dish/meat-jun"],["Morkovcha","dish/morkovcha"],["Scorched rice","dish/scorched-rice"],["Seon (food)","dish/seon-food"],["Sungnyung","dish/sungnyung"],["Tteokbokki","dish/tteokbokki"],["Wakame","dish/wakame"],["Yakgwa","dish/yakgwa"],["Yukpo","dish/yukpo"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f8/Meju_%28fermented_soybean%29.jpg/500px-Meju_%28fermented_soybean%29.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"mspphoto","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meju_(fermented_soybean).jpg"}},"dish/menchi-katsu":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/menchi-katsu","n":"Menchi-katsu","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Yoshoku","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Menchi-katsu is a Japanese breaded and deep-fried ground meat patty: a fried meat cake. The meat is usually ground beef, pork, or a mixture of the two. It is often served in inexpensive bento and teishoku. Menchi-katsu is also used as a sandwich filling."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-menchi-katsu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menchi-katsu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yoshoku","cuisine/yoshoku"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Panko","ingredient/panko"]]},{"h":"More from Yoshoku","links":[["Chicken katsu","dish/chicken-katsu"],["Cream stew","dish/cream-stew"],["Doria (food)","dish/doria-food"],["Hayashi rice","dish/hayashi-rice"],["Naporitan","dish/naporitan"],["Tonkatsu","dish/tonkatsu"],["Toruko rice","dish/toruko-rice"],["Volga rice","dish/volga-rice"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/1/16/Menchi_%28minced_pork%29_katsu.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Hajime NAKANO (jetalone)","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Menchi_(minced_pork)_katsu.jpg"}},"dish/nasi-kucing":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/nasi-kucing","n":"Nasi kucing","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Nasi kucing is an Indonesian rice dish that originated in Central Java, primarily in the Yogyakarta, Semarang, and Surakarta areas but has since spread throughout the country. It consists of a small portion of rice with toppings, usually sambal, dried fish, and tempeh, wrapped in banana leaves."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-nasi-kucing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nasi_kucing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Sambal","ingredient/sambal"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9d/Nasi_kucing_langgi.jpg/500px-Nasi_kucing_langgi.jpg","w":500,"h":295,"by":"Crisco 1492","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasi_kucing_langgi.jpg"}},"dish/paccheri":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/paccheri","n":"Paccheri","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Paccheri is a type of pasta in the shape of a very large tube, originating from the Campania region of Italy. They are generally smooth, but there is also a ribbed version, paccheri millerighe. The name comes from Neapolitan paccharia, 'slaps', with a depreciative -ero suffix (-eri in plural) to indicate something common. The name has been ascribed to a slapping sound they may make when eaten. They can be served stuffed, and are commonly prepared with beans, or with ricotta and tomato sauce in Campania. As they are eaten, they split open, forming a flat sheet. In the late 1990s, food writer Arthur Schwartz described paccharia as the most popular large tube pasta in Campania."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-paccheri"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paccheri"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Durum wheat","ingredient/durum-wheat"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Manu's Menu","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalha